==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|þrír|lang=is}}, from {{etyl|gmq-pro|is}} {{term|lang=gmq-pro|ᚦᚱᛁᛃᛟᛉ|tr=þrijoz}} {{qualifier|feminine plural}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*þrīz}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*tréyes}}. Compare Faroese ''[[tríggir]]'', Norwegian, Swedish, and Danish {{term|tre|lang=da}}.

===Cardinal number===
'''þrír''' {{g|m-p}}, '''[[þrjár]]''' {{g|f-p}}, '''[[þrjú]]''' {{g|n-p}}

# '''[[three]]'''; the cardinal number after [[tveir#Icelandic|tveir]] and before [[fjórir#Icelandic|fjórir]].

====Declension====
{{is-numeral (þrír)|}}

====Related terms====
* (''ordinal form'') [[þriðji]] {{g|m}}, [[þriðja]] {{g|f|n}}

====Derived terms====
* [[klukkan þrjú]]

